o converge in the 750-850 range. Plan_021 with trained embeddings shows one seed already done with extreme NVE peaking at 14.59x, and I'm predicting collapse across all three seeds.\n\nNow I'm clarifying the distinction—plan_021 is actually the CIVO trigger configuration with trained embeddings and subsampling enabled, while plan_022 is the control without the embedding dimension. Looking at plan_021, I expect 2 out of 3 seeds to collapse with NVE peaks ranging from 8-15x, though one seed might self-correct. Plan_022 as the control shows noisier NVE peaks between 1.3-2.0x, not as clean as what I saw with Walker. Plan_023 with untrained embeddings appears directionally consistent with Walker's behavior, showing value suppression but the thought trails off there.\n\nScanning through the remaining analyses, plan_030 confirms the RSSM prediction fidelity gap, plan_031 shows entropy patterns with some noise, and plan_032 reveals clear value prediction separation though with some overlap. The dt_embedding cosine similarity in plan_033 shows trained embeddings diverging but isn't strongly diagnostic. Plan_034's threshold sensitivity analysis suggests around 80-85% accuracy at the 1.5x threshold before dropping due to borderline cases. The Cartpole experiments won't finish in time given only 2 environments were completed. Plan_060 on uncertainty-gated truncation shows promising pilot results.\n\nFor plan_040 on Hopper, that's priority 2 and won't run before the deadline. I'm also noticing 018v2 and 008f_s3 in the registry that weren't explicitly listed in the plan—018v2 is currently analyzing and 008f_s3 is preparing. Looking back at the median tier hypotheses, these actually do contain relevant findings about NVE thresholds and their relationship to performance recovery, so I should factor those in rather than skip them.\n\nBut the user specifically asked for predictions on each planned experiment in the plan, so I need to stick to those entries with \"planned\" status rat